# The DynamoDB-compatible service module (services/dynamodb/,
# .kiro/specs/dynamodb-compatible-api/). Sourced from the top-level
# Kconfig's "Service Modules" menu.

config DYNAMODB
	bool "DynamoDB-compatible API (tables, items, indexes, streams)"
	default n
	depends on OPENSSL
	help
	  Builds the services/dynamodb/ module: a DynamoDB-compatible service
	  that unmodified AWS SDKs, the AWS CLI, KCL, the DynamoDB lock client
	  and the Streams Kinesis Adapter can point --endpoint-url at. Items
	  live in the persistent-state-machine kv_engine: the in-memory engine
	  is always built, and RocksDB is used where that spec's engine is on.

	  So far the module holds the pinned botocore models of DynamoDB and
	  DynamoDB Streams, their generated shape tables for the core AWS JSON
	  codec (include/raft/aws_json_protocol.hpp), the operation coverage
	  test and the recorded client wire evidence (task 1). The codecs,
	  state machines, front end and dynamodb_gateway_node follow.

	  OpenSSL is needed for SigV4 (the core sigv4_verifier). It uses
	  IAM's core headers but not the IAM module. Off by default like every
	  new module (services/README.md). See
	  .kiro/specs/dynamodb-compatible-api/.

config DYNAMODB_GATEWAY_IAM
	bool "IAM authentication in dynamodb_gateway_node"
	default y
	depends on DYNAMODB && IAM
	help
	  Builds dynamodb_gateway_node with an embedded read replica of the
	  IAM Raft group and IAM's authorizer, so KYTHIRA_DYNAMODB_AUTH=iam or
	  both authenticates and authorizes requests against Kythira IAM with
	  no network call. Configured by the KYTHIRA_IAM_* variables. The
	  DynamoDB module itself never includes IAM: only the daemon's
	  composition root does. See .kiro/specs/dynamodb-compatible-api/
	  task 28.
